 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? That's a great thing to support. You don' need to be fluent. simple yes, no, and few basics go a long way. I' tested it with my own kids. A few basic phrases and body language carry lot. Let her. Ask her to teach you one word a day, and practice saying it differently, like a pirate or an astronaut. Probably at first, but she' start picking it up. You could also find a short picture book in French and read it together. There are simple French games activities you can do together. A French word of day picture card deck is great for little ones.",
